\mt1 2 John
\c 1
\s1 A Greeting from the Elder
\r (\ref 3 John 1:1–4|3JN 1-4\ref*)
\p \v 1 The elder,
\p To \add the\add* chosen lady and her children, whom I love in \add the\add* truth — and not I alone, but also all who know the truth — \v 2 because of the truth that abides in us and will be with us forever:
\p \v 3 Grace, mercy, \add and\add* peace from God \add the\add* Father and from Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, will be with us in truth and love.
\s1 Walking in the Truth
\r (\ref John 8:30–47|JHN 8:30-47\ref*)
\p \v 4 I was overjoyed to find \add some\add* of your children walking in \add the\add* truth, just as the Father has commanded \add us\add*. \v 5 And now I urge you, \add dear\add* lady — not as a new commandment to you, but \add one\add* we have had from \add the\add* beginning — that we love one another. \v 6 And this is love, that we walk according to His commandments. This is the very commandment you have heard from \add the\add* beginning, that you must walk in \add love\add*.
\s1 Beware of Deceivers
\p \v 7 For many deceivers have gone out into the world, refusing to confess the coming of Jesus Christ in \add the\add* flesh. Any such \add person \add* is the deceiver and the antichrist. \v 8 Watch yourselves, so that you do not lose what we have worked for,\f + \fr 1:8 \ft NE and WH \fqa what you have worked for\f* but \add that\add* you may be fully rewarded. \v 9 Anyone who runs ahead without remaining in the teaching of Christ does not have God. Whoever remains in \add His\add* teaching has both the Father and the Son.
\p \v 10 If anyone comes to you \add but\add* does not bring this teaching, \add do\add* not receive him into \add your\add* home \add or\add* even greet him. \v 11 Whoever greets \add such a person\add* shares in his evil deeds.
\s1 Conclusion
\r (\ref 3 John 1:13–14|3JN 13-14\ref*)
\p \v 12 I have many things to write to you, \add but\add* I would prefer not \add to do so\add* with paper and ink. Instead, I hope to come and speak with you \add face\add* to \add face\add*,\f + \fr 1:12 \ft Literally \fqa mouth to mouth\f* so that our joy may be complete.
\p \v 13 The children of your elect sister send you greetings.\f + \fr 1:13 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa Amen.\f*
